    "title": {
      "en": "WoW Token Price Hits 640k Gold Spike on EU Servers",
      "es": "El precio de la ficha de WoW alcanza un pico de 640 000 de oro en los servidores de la UE"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "WoW Token Price Hits 640k Gold Spike on EU Servers...",
      "es": "El precio de la ficha de WoW alcanza un pico de 640 000 de oro en los servidores de la UE..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6afbbf38a48ad0.56216079\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">The WoW Token price has spiked in both regions over the last couple of days, with the trading price reaching a peak of 640k gold on EU servers.<br><br>Over the last couple of days, but particularly in the last couple of hours, the WoW Token price has peaked on both NA and EU servers. Some players have speculated that the price is so high due to Retail content being in a lull with the launch of Forever, and while a portion of this might be true for previous days, the main cause of today's spike is likely that <a href=\"https://eu.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/wow-token-in-game-shop-error-cannot-buy-wow-token/643357/9\" data-contiguous=\"true\" target=\"_blank\">WoW Tokens were unable to be purchased</a>.<hr>On EU servers, the WoW Token price hit a new peak of just over 640k gold for a single token. According to <a href=\"https://wowtoken.app/\" data-contiguous=\"true\" target=\"_blank\">WoW Token App</a>, a WoW Token tracking website, this is a 100k spike over yesterday. The price of the WoW Token started to increase around the time WoW: Forever launched, but has seen a massive increase within the last 24 hours.<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1309094.png\" id=\"1309094\"><img width=\"800\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1309094.png?maxWidth=800\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image\" alt=\"EU Gold Spike\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 2.04459 / 1;\"></a> <br><i>Image from <a href=\"https://wowtoken.app/\" data-contiguous=\"true\" target=\"_blank\">WoW Token App</a> - EU 3 Months</i></div><br><br>The NA token has also seen a similar spike, but not nearly to the same raw gold amount. The WoW Token for NA servers is around 375k gold per token currently. <br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1309097.png\" id=\"1309097\"><img width=\"800\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1309097.png?maxWidth=800\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image\" alt=\"NA Gold Spike\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 2.0478 / 1;\"></a> <br><i>Image from <a href=\"https://wowtoken.app/\" data-contiguous=\"true\" target=\"_blank\">WoW Token App</a> - NA 3 Months</i></div><br><br>Some players who have been looking for Gold, potentially for the <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/new-limited-time-5-million-gold-mount-includes-customizable-vendors-in-patch-12-382733\" data-contiguous=\"true\">new 5 Million Gold mount</a>, might be looking to get a WoW Token for some gold, with the price being so high. Alternatively, if you were wanting to buy game time with Retail gold, you may wish to hold off, as prices are coming down with the shop issues having been fixed.</div>\n            \n            <noscript>The WoW Token price has spiked in both regions over the last couple of days, with the trading price reaching a peak of 640k gold on EU servers.<br /><br />Over the last couple of days, but particularly in the last couple of hours, the WoW Token price has peaked on both NA and EU servers. Some players have speculated that the price is so high due to Retail content being in a lull with the launch of Forever, and while a portion of this might be true for previous days, the main cause of today's spike is likely that <a href=\"https://eu.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/wow-token-in-game-shop-error-cannot-buy-wow-token/643357/9\" rel=\"nofollow\">WoW Tokens were unable to be purchased</a>. <br /><br />On EU servers, the WoW Token price hit a new peak of just over 640k gold for a single token. According to <a href=\"https://wowtoken.app/\" rel=\"nofollow\">WoW Token App</a>, a WoW Token tracking website, this is a 100k spike over yesterday. The price of the WoW Token started to increase around the time WoW: Forever launched, but has seen a massive increase within the last 24 hours.<br /><br /><i>Image from <a href=\"https://wowtoken.app/\" rel=\"nofollow\">WoW Token App</a> - EU 3 Months</i><br /><br />The NA token has also seen a similar spike, but not nearly to the same raw gold amount. The WoW Token for NA servers is around 375k gold per token currently. <br /><br /><i>Image from <a href=\"https://wowtoken.app/\" rel=\"nofollow\">WoW Token App</a> - NA 3 Months</i><br /><br />Some players who have been looking for Gold, potentially for the <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/new-limited-time-5-million-gold-mount-includes-customizable-vendors-in-patch-12-382733\">new 5 Million Gold mount</a>, might be looking to get a WoW Token for some gold, with the price being so high. Alternatively, if you were wanting to buy game time with Retail gold, you may wish to hold off, as prices are coming down with the shop issues having been fixed.</noscript>            \n        ",
